---
title: "feat: initial forehead implementation — Rust tool for license headers"

doc:
  - audience: Developer
    description: |
      Initial implementation of forehead, a Rust tool for creating and
      maintaining file headers for code license. Includes:

      - forehead-core: library crate with config, template, comment, and
        header modules (publishable on crates.io)
      - forehead-cli: CLI binary with apply, check, list, init commands
      - Supports 30+ file types with correct comment style detection
      - forehead.toml config with path-based mapping rules
      - Template placeholders: {project}, {author}, {year}, {year_span},
        {license}, {repository}, {description}, {file}
      - CI/CD pipeline: fmt -> clippy -> test -> build
      - Dual-licensed: Apache-2.0 OR MIT

crates:
  - name: forehead-core
    bump: minor
  - name: forehead-cli
    bump: minor
---